    "turn_text": "everybody remembers the Alamo. But there are missions in El Paso. that are older than the Alamo. When you look at a place like Fort Davis that has McDonald's Observatory, when I was in school, when I was in science class in eighth, ninth, tenth grade, we learned that the universe had expanded after the big band and was contracting. What they learned at McDonald's Observatory was actually the universe is accelerating in its expansion. Because of a thing called dark energy which the universe is made of like 70% And we still don't know what dark energy is right like that's going on in in Fort Davis, Texas And then big bend you know in Santa Elena Canyon is is one of the most majestic things I've ever gotten the scene And so those are some of the things that I've enjoyed representing such a big district. And if that just means I put 90,000 miles on my car, I'll put 90,000 miles on my car for that. What's the car? A Jeep Grand Cherokee. Well, it can handle that. Yeah, it can. It can.",
