  {
    "episode_id": 82928,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82928.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 44,
    "turn_text": "I can only speak from my district. And the answer is no. The answer is, and you even had a Democratic court. say that Latino voters in the 23rd district were not being marginalized. And part of that is because I'm out there representing them. And ultimately, when the margins of victory in a lot of places are not that wide. And so people have to be motivated to come out and exercise their right to vote.",
