    "turn_text": "No, I don't think it has anything to do with my race. I do not believe in coattails. I do not believe in national trends. If you let national trends affect you, the national trends will affect you. But I have an independent relationship with my district and people know me and they know that whether You're a town that votes overwhelmingly Democrat. When you have a flood... And you need help from FEMA? Guess what? I'm going to be there. I'm going to help you. But if you're somebody who doesn't go home on the weekends, who is not out in your community, who does not reach out to parts of the community that may not naturally be open to your party's brand, then yeah, you're gonna get impacted by national trends. But if you have your own relationship, you're gonna be fine. When do you vote on the tax bill? It's today. and you're going to vote for it. I'm going to vote for it. Yeah, because look, in my district, 81% of the district fills out the 1040 easy. And that basically means you don't take any deductions. So the fact that the standard deduction is doubled means a lot of people are going to have, it means everybody who does that is going to have more money in their",
