    "turn_idx": 85,
    "turn_text": "So I justified both votes because my goal on health care is to increase access to and decrease cost of health care. When it comes to the individual mandates, if you don't have insurance, you can pay a fine. And the number of folks that were actually paying the fine was significantly higher than the folks that wrote this bill thought was going to happen. And the people that were disproportionately doing the fine were younger folks. And so this is saying, and this goes back to should the government dictate whether everybody has to have insurance or not. That's the core of this debate for many people. I don't think that the government should dictate whether or not you buy insurance.",
