  {
    "episode_id": 82928,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82928.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 153,
    "turn_text": "So I would say I think some of the voices that have been in the opposition of him have not been amplified. They sometimes are overlooked. The Speaker of the House, the Majority Leader of the Senate, have oftentimes disagreed with the president. That doesn't get the level of focus. But guess what? My responsibility and my job is to continue to be honest, treat people with respect, agree when I agree and disagree when I disagree. And that's how I'm going to continue to operate. And again, folks sometimes want to act like the president's my boss. No. I have 800,000 bosses. And they're in 29 counties back in the Lone Star state, all right? And those are the people, those are the people that I listen to. And for me, yeah, of course at times it's frustrating. But guess what? I'm also a voice and a wing of the Republican Party. And for us, this experiment called America has worked because of the competition of ideas. And we should also look and to amplify the message of someone on the other party that we agree with. And that is something that sometimes always gets lost. When did it happen that the most important thing in our life is the political party we identify with? This wasn't the case when I was a kid. What happened to recognizing that, hey, even though you may wear different team jerseys than I do, that doesn't mean you're bad. And that requires all of us to start thinking that way. So that's something that, if I can prove that point, I'm going to continue to prove that point, but I'm going to be myself and do what my daddy always said, be honest. And I'm going to do what my mom always said, and that's be kind to people.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
